Search for "higgsfield mcp" and you will find a dozen setup posts that all skip the same question: what else can an AI assistant reach through MCP when you want images, video, voice and design, and what does each option really cost once the credits run out? In the last two months nearly every creative platform has shipped a hosted connector for Claude, ChatGPT or Cursor, and the details differ in ways that matter: who needs an API key, which plan unlocks which tool, whether the server is official, and whether "unlimited" survives the trip through MCP.

This guide compares ten options: Higgsfield, fal, Replicate, Runway, ElevenLabs, Luma, Kling, Stability AI, Canva and the OpenAI image tooling. Short version: Higgsfield is the most complete studio you can drive from chat, fal is the best pick for developers who want hundreds of models behind one OAuth login, and a few names on the list (Stability AI, Kling, OpenAI) do not ship the kind of hosted generation server their brand suggests, so we say exactly what exists instead. Every price below is dated November 26, 2026.

{% youtube id="RNpoF1c44u0" title="How To Connect Claude + Higgsfield To Create Real AI Videos | Complete Tutorial" /%}

*A third-party Higgsfield and Claude walkthrough from the Mo Decodes AI channel (title confirmed through YouTube oEmbed on November 26, 2026). Menus and plans change quickly, so use the written steps and pricing tables below for current details.*

## Short answer: quick picks

- **Best overall for creators working inside a chat:** [Higgsfield](https://higgsfield.ai/mcp). One connector for image, video, characters, audio and ad workflows, with official routes into Claude, ChatGPT and Cursor. The catch is that MCP always spends credits and needs a paid subscription.
- **Best for developers and the widest model catalog:** [fal](https://fal.ai/docs/documentation/setting-up/mcp). One OAuth login, no API key in your client, a one-line installer for nine coding agents, and per-model pricing you can check before you generate.
- **Best free way to try:** ElevenLabs (a $0 plan with 10,000 credits per month, per its pricing page) or Stability AI's 25 free API credits. Higgsfield's Free plan carries no monthly credits.
- **Best open source:** Replicate's `replicate-mcp` npm package, or the community Stability server (MIT licence, but last pushed in June 2025).
- **Best for ad variants from one product photo:** Luma's connector, which wraps preset workflows such as product shots, camera angles, background swap and relight.

{% callout type="warning" %}
Credits are the real cost of every server on this list. Higgsfield's help center states that MCP "always uses credits" regardless of plan, ElevenLabs warns that retrying a running generation starts and charges a new one, and fal's docs say the "ask for approval first" prompt is a request to the model, not a server-side approval gate. Set a spending cap on the vendor side before you give an agent a long task.
{% /callout %}

