## Head-to-head: which to pick

### Higgsfield vs fal

Pick Higgsfield if you want finished workflows (ads from a product link, character consistency, motion transfer) and are happy with a monthly subscription. Pick fal if you want to choose among many models, see a price before each run and pay only for outputs. Higgsfield's connector bills credits from a plan; fal's draws prepaid credits per model. Both use OAuth, both have official routes into Claude, ChatGPT and Cursor, and both warn that generation spends money. If you are undecided, connect fal first: there is no subscription to cancel.

### Runway vs Luma

Runway's generation server is a general video tool with a free plan and a $15 entry price. Luma's connector is narrower and more opinionated: product shots, camera angles, background swap and relight, from $30 a month. Pick Luma when the job is "one product photo into a set of ads." Pick Runway when you want open-ended clips and a cheap way to test.

## How to connect: Claude, ChatGPT and Cursor

These steps come from each client's own documentation, dated November 26, 2026. Client menus move often; Claude's docs and fal's docs both note that "Settings" and "Customize" labels have changed, so look for Connectors or Plugins if a label differs.

{% figure src="https://static.higgsfield.ai/landing/gpt-skills/20261016-assets/demos/fashion.webp" alt="Fashion editorial image generated through Higgsfield's MCP connector, from a prompt shown on the MCP page" caption="A sample result shown on Higgsfield's MCP page for the prompt 'Create a fashion editorial photo...'. Source: higgsfield.ai/mcp" /%}

### Claude (claude.ai and Claude Desktop)

Per Claude's help article on custom connectors, for an individual Pro or Max plan:

1. Open **Customize** then **Connectors**.
2. Click **+ Add**, then **Add custom connector**.
3. Enter a name (this is what you see in the list).
4. Paste the remote MCP server URL exactly as the vendor documents it, including the path.
5. Click **Continue**, review the authentication settings Claude detected, then **Continue** again.
6. Choose how people connect (for example **Sign in now**), complete the browser sign-in, and approve.
7. In a new chat, click **+**, open **Connectors**, and switch the connector on.

On Team and Enterprise plans an organization owner adds the connector first, under Organization settings, Connectors. Vendor-specific notes:

| Server | Name | URL to paste | Source |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| Higgsfield | Higgsfield | `https://mcp.higgsfield.ai/mcp` | Higgsfield help center and MCP page |
| fal | fal | `https://mcp.fal.ai/mcp-relay` | fal docs |
| ElevenLabs | ElevenLabs | `https://api.elevenlabs.io/v1/mcp` | ElevenLabs docs |
| Luma | Luma AI | `https://agents.lumalabs.ai/mcp` | Pre-filled by the Luma "Add to Claude" button |
| Replicate | Replicate | `https://mcp.replicate.com/sse` (needs an API token) | Replicate hosted MCP page |
| Runway (generation) | Runway | `https://mcp.runwayml.com/mcp` | mcp.runwayml.com |

### ChatGPT

OpenAI's developer docs say ChatGPT connects custom MCP servers as plugins, on the web, with workspace permissions and Lockdown applying:

1. Go to ChatGPT Plugins at chatgpt.com/plugins.
2. Select the plus button, then **Add custom MCP server**.
3. Enter a name and optional description. Under **Connection**, enter the Server URL.
4. Configure authentication (OAuth, no authentication, or both).
5. Review the risk warning and select **I understand and want to continue**.
6. Select **Create as a plugin**, then install the plugin before using it in a conversation.

OpenAI lists the supported protocols as SSE and streaming HTTP. Before you paste a URL, check whether the vendor offers an official plugin, which is simpler:

- **Higgsfield:** use the official Higgsfield plugin from the Plugins Directory (the help center says ChatGPT uses the plugin instead of a manual URL). Audio generation and the Website Building skill are not available there.
- **fal:** open the fal plugin listing, select Install plugin, connect and sign in, then type `@fal`.
- **Luma:** search for Luma AI at chatgpt.com/plugins, install, sign in, then type `@Luma AI` and attach a product photo.
- **Canva:** a third-party guide (connectorsguide.com) describes adding `https://mcp.canva.com/mcp` as a custom connector with Developer mode. Check Canva's own listing for an official plugin.

### Cursor

Cursor's MCP docs show that a remote server needs only a `url` entry in `mcp.json`, and static OAuth credentials can be added when a provider needs them. Cursor documents `~/.cursor/mcp.json` for all projects and `.cursor/mcp.json` per project.

1. Open the Cursor Marketplace (Customize, then Marketplace) and look for Higgsfield or fal. Click Add and sign in. This is the officially documented route for both.
2. Or edit `~/.cursor/mcp.json` and merge an entry, preserving your other servers:

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "fal": { "url": "https://mcp.fal.ai/mcp-relay" },
    "Runway Dev": { "url": "https://dev.runwayml.com/mcp" }
  }
}
```

3. Open Cursor's MCP settings, find the server and complete browser sign-in. Each user authorizes their own connection.
4. In an Agent chat, ask Cursor to find a model without running it, as fal's docs suggest, to confirm the connection before you spend credits.

