## How we evaluated

We worked from primary sources on November 26, 2026: vendor pricing pages, official MCP docs, help centers and changelog or news posts, plus the client docs for Claude, ChatGPT and Cursor. We fetched each page, recorded prices as shown, and checked every URL in this article for an HTTP response. We verified the YouTube video through YouTube's oEmbed endpoint, the X posts through X's syndication endpoint, and the images with `curl -I` for status and content type. We checked GitHub's API for the community Stability server.

## FAQ

### What is the Higgsfield MCP URL?

Higgsfield's help center gives `https://mcp.higgsfield.ai/mcp` as the connector URL, and the MCP page's "Add Higgsfield to Claude" button uses the same address. In ChatGPT, use the official Higgsfield plugin instead of a URL, and in Cursor use the marketplace entry.

### How do I use Higgsfield MCP in Claude?

Open Customize, then Connectors, choose Add custom connector, name it Higgsfield, paste the URL, click Connect, then sign in and authorize on Higgsfield. You need an active Higgsfield subscription. Credits are deducted for every generation.

### Is Higgsfield MCP free?

Not in a durable way. The Free plan has no monthly credits, MCP always deducts credits, and the help center lists an active subscription as a prerequisite. Higgsfield's November 18 MCP 2.0 post advertised a free 3-day trial with unlimited generations, which conflicts with the help-center rules, so confirm the current offer on the page.

### How can I use Higgsfield AI for free?

On higgsfield.ai the Free plan allows limited access to selected models, one generation at a time, with no monthly credits. That is website use, not MCP. For a free way to test an MCP workflow with real output, ElevenLabs' $0 plan or Stability's 25 free credits are better fits.

### Do I need an API key for these servers?

For Higgsfield, fal, Runway, ElevenLabs, Luma and Canva, the documentation describes OAuth sign-in with no API key in the client. Replicate's hosted and local servers need an API token, and the community Stability server needs a Stability API key.

### What is the difference between fal's MCP and its Platform MCP?

The model-generation server at `https://mcp.fal.ai/mcp-relay` finds models and runs generations. fal's docs describe a separate Platform MCP for account operations and serverless debugging, and a documentation-only MCP that does not touch your account.

### Does Stability AI have an official MCP server for image generation?

We found only an official docs server at `https://docs.stability.ai/mcp`, which cannot generate images. The generation option we found is a community project, `tadasant/mcp-server-stability-ai`, which says it is not affiliated with Stability AI and was last pushed on June 24, 2025.

### Does OpenAI have an image MCP server?

We did not find one. OpenAI documents an `image_generation` tool in the Responses API with GPT Image models, and the Responses API can also call remote MCP servers. Those are separate features.

### Why does Runway have two MCP servers?

One generates media in chat (`mcp.runwayml.com/mcp`), the other connects a coding agent to your Developer Portal account (`dev.runwayml.com/mcp`).

### Can I reach Kling through MCP today?

Kling published an MCP guide, but we could not read a server URL from it. Kling models are listed on fal, Runway and Higgsfield, which you can connect now.

### Are MCP servers safe to connect to my account?

OpenAI's docs warn that an untrusted server can access information or trick the model into unintended actions, including changing or deleting data. Use official URLs, OAuth, per-tool toggles and vendor-side spend caps, and be careful with community servers that hold an API key.

